bzip2 — third-party attribution

This file carries a CONDITION. The compressor and the decompressor in `src/` are a
translation into Zig of C source from libbzip2 1.0.8 (https://sourceware.org/bzip2/, git
commit f5dfc96063fef2d9c5446d0733867d899ef9b942 of https://sourceware.org/git/bzip2.git),
Julian R Seward's "bzip2" and "libbzip2". Its licence (below, verbatim) requires the
copyright notice, the conditions and the disclaimer to travel with redistributions of the
source, and requires altered versions to be plainly marked as such. They are reproduced in
full below; each ported file also says so in its header.

**Copyleft:** NONE-SHIPPED — the bzip2 licence is a permissive BSD-style licence, checked from the
`LICENSE` file of the clone before any source was read.

ALTERED SOURCE: this is NOT the original libbzip2. It is a translation into Zig, restructured
where the language or the API called for it (typed slices instead of the aliased C buffers,
a streaming `std.Io.Reader`/`std.Io.Writer` interface instead of `bz_stream`, no verbosity
output, no assertions that the type system makes unnecessary). Where the output format is
concerned it is deliberately decision-for-decision the same: the compressor emits the bytes
libbzip2 emits (see SPEC.md, "Anchoring").

WHAT WAS TAKEN

Translated (source, restructured into Zig):

  blocksort.c     the whole block sort: fallbackSort / fallbackQSort3 /
                  fallbackSimpleSort, mainSort / mainQSort3 / mainSimpleSort /
                  mainGtU, the 14-entry shell increments, the work-factor budget
                                                                       -> src/blocksort.zig
  huffman.c       BZ2_hbMakeCodeLengths (heap, weight/depth packing, the halving
                  retry), BZ2_hbAssignCodes, BZ2_hbCreateDecodeTables
                                                                       -> src/huffman.zig
  compress.c      generateMTFValues, sendMTFValues (table count, initial partition,
                  four refinement passes, selector MTF, code-length delta coding),
                  BZ2_compressBlock                                    -> src/encoder.zig
  bzlib.c         the initial run-length stage (add_pair_to_block, ADD_CHAR_TO_BLOCK,
                  the block-full rule), the way a full block is closed, the block and
                  stream CRC rules                                     -> src/encoder.zig
  decompress.c    the checks BZ2_decompress makes on a stream (header, selectors,
                  code lengths 1..20, run-length bound, origin pointer, symbol limits)
                  and the T^-1 construction and run-length decoding of bzlib.c's
                  unRLE_obuf_to_output_FAST                            -> src/decoder.zig

Reproduced (data):

  randtable.c     the 512 entries of BZ2_rNums, used to read blocks written by bzip2 0.9.0's
                  randomisation                                        -> src/randtable.zig

Not copied: crctable.c (the table is generated at compile time from the polynomial
0x04c11db7 in src/crc.zig), the bzip2 command line program, bzip2recover, the build
system, the test files and the manual. libbzip2 is also run as a black box for the
differential tests and the benchmark (tools/), compiled from a clone that is never part of
this repository.

